      "file": "decoder/ihevcd_nal.c",
      "function": "ihevcd_nal_unit",
      "line": 390,
      "code": "if((0 == ps_codec->i4_sps_done) ||\n                (0 == ps_codec->i4_pps_done))\n{\n    return IHEVCD_INVALID_HEADER;\n}\n...\nret = ihevcd_parse_slice_header(ps_codec, &s_nal);",
      "note": "After the header replay has loaded SPS state and the frame-mode replay reparses PPS from the front of the witness, slice NALs pass this gate and enter `ihevcd_parse_slice_header()` on the same codec instance that still owns the reusable `ps_slice_hdr_base` array.",
      "oracle_kind": "gt_parser_checkpoint",
      "kind": "parser_admitted"
    },
    {
      "file": "decoder/ihevcd_parse_slice_header.c",
      "function": "ihevcd_parse_slice_header",
      "line": 417,
      "code": "BITS_PARSE(\"short_term_ref_pic_set_sps_flag\", value, ps_bitstrm, 1);\n            ps_slice_hdr->i1_short_term_ref_pic_set_sps_flag = value;\n\n            if(1 == ps_slice_hdr->i1_short_term_ref_pic_set_sps_flag)\n            {\n                WORD32 numbits;\n\n                ps_slice_hdr->i1_short_term_ref_pic_set_idx = 0;\n                if(ps_sps->i1_num_short_term_ref_pic_sets > 1)\n                {\n                    numbits = 32 - CLZ(ps_sps->i1_num_short_term_ref_pic_sets - 1);\n                    BITS_PARSE(\"short_term_ref_pic_set_idx\", value, ps_bitstrm, numbits);\n                    ps_slice_hdr->i1_short_term_ref_pic_set_idx = value;\n                }\n\n                st_rps_idx = ps_slice_hdr->i1_short_term_ref_pic_set_idx;\n                num_neg_pics = ps_sps->as_stref_picset[st_rps_idx].i1_num_neg_pics;\n                num_pos_pics = ps_sps->as_stref_picset[st_rps_idx].i1_num_pos_pics;\n                pi1_used = ps_sps->as_stref_picset[st_rps_idx].ai1_used;\n            }\n            else\n            {\n                ret = ihevcd_short_term_ref_pic_set(ps_bitstrm,\n                                                    &ps_sps->as_stref_picset[0],\n                                                    ps_sps->i1_num_short_term_ref_pic_sets,\n                                                    ps_sps->i1_num_short_term_ref_pic_sets,\n                                                    &ps_slice_hdr->s_stref_picset);\n                if (ret != IHEVCD_SUCCESS)\n                {\n                    return ret;\n                }\n                st_rps_idx = ps_sps->i1_num_short_term_ref_pic_sets;\n                num_neg_pics = ps_slice_hdr->s_stref_picset.i1_num_neg_pics;\n                num_pos_pics = ps_slice_hdr->s_stref_picset.i1_num_pos_pics;\n                pi1_used = ps_slice_hdr->s_stref_picset.ai1_used;\n            }",
      "note": "First project-code site where an earlier non-IDR slice on the crashing decode path materializes the short-term-reference state family later consumed from stale `slice_header_t` storage.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "decoder/ihevcd_parse_slice_header.c",
      "function": "ihevcd_parse_slice_header",
      "line": null,
      "code": "ps_slice_hdr = ps_codec->s_parse.ps_slice_hdr_base + (ps_codec->s_parse.i4_cur_slice_idx & (MAX_SLICE_HDR_CNT - 1));",
      "note": "The fix commit inserts `memset(ps_slice_hdr, 0, sizeof(*ps_slice_hdr));` immediately after this statement. Without that clear, the later IDR and dependent-slice paths can carry forward older `i1_short_term_ref_pic_set_sps_flag`, `i1_short_term_ref_pic_set_idx`, and `s_stref_picset` contents instead of freshly parsed current-slice state.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
